#
# PAM configuration for the swaylock screen locker, with face unlock (Howdy with
# the IR camera) tried before the password. See docs/face-unlock.md.
#
# Install as /etc/pam.d/swaylock. On Debian this file is a dpkg conffile, so keep
# a copy of the original and keep the local version when an upgrade asks.
# The stock file is just "auth include login".
#
# On the lock screen, press Enter with an empty password and look at the screen.
# If no face matches before Howdy's timeout, type the password as usual.
# swaylock runs as the locked user, so that user must be able to open the camera
# (group "video") and read /etc/howdy and its models.
auth sufficient /usr/local/lib/security/pam_howdy.so
auth include login
